BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  In the age of the First Dawn, two weavers, Elara and Kael, tended the loom of existence. Elara) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (     possessed five golden threads of potential. She could hoard them, keeping their luster dim,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (     or she could cast them into the Great Loom, where the divine fire would triple their count.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (     But the Loom required a second hand-Kael's.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  Elara chose to cast her threads forward, trusting Kael to weave them into a tapestry of shared) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (     prosperity. When the Loom roared, the threads became fifteen, glowing with warmth. Kael, st) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    anding at the precipice of greed, caught the threads. He knew that for the tapestry to hold,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (     he must cast back a portion of the fire to Elara, ensuring they both walked away with more ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (    than they began.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  They played this dance across the eons. When Elara sent all, and Kael returned fairly, the tap) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    estry grew until it blanketed the world in light. But when suspicion took root, the threads ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    withered, and the loom fell silent. They learned that the secret to a thriving kingdom was n) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    ot the threads themselves, but the courage to pass them on, knowing the other would honor th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    e weave. Trust was the loom; reciprocity was the cloth.) Tj ET
