BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  In the beginning, two weavers, Aethel and Thorne, sat at the Great Loom. Aethel held the silve) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (    r thread, a finite resource of five strands. Thorne sat opposite, guarding the empty frame. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    Aethel knew that to cast her silver into the void was risky, yet the Loom possessed a divine) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (     alchemy: whatever was passed through the golden eye tripled in length.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  If Aethel withheld her silver, fearing the silence of the loom, the cloth remained gray and br) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    ittle. But when she cast her threads to Thorne, the Loom hummed, turning three silver strand) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    s into nine. Thorne, standing at the precipice of choice, held the power to hoard the bounty) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (     or return the favor. If Thorne returned half, the cycle reinforced itself, building a tapes) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    try that could outlast the stars.) Tj ET
