BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      In the beginning, the world was barren, until Aethel, the Giver, descended with a single h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        andful of golden grain. He met Mura, the Keeper of the Earth, at the threshold of the gr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        eat garden. Aethel knew that if he cast his grain upon the soil, the earth would yield a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (         harvest three times its measure. Yet, he hesitated, for the choice of how to divide the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (         bounty rested solely with Mura.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      "I offer you this light," Aethel whispered, scattering the grains into the dark soil. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        earth trembled, and at once, the harvest tripled, blooming into a bounty of abundance. M) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        ura stood over the golden stalks, the weight of power heavy in her hands. To keep it all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (         was to invite the winter of isolation; to return a measure to Aethel was to weave a tap) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        estry of trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      Mura watched the Giver's expectant eyes. She understood that life was not a mere tally of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        coins, but a dance of mutual grace. With a gentle sigh, she pressed half the harvest bac) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (        k into Aethel's waiting palm. From that day, the garden never failed, for it was nourish) Tj ET
