BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        ted by the law of reciprocity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      If Elara kept her seeds, the orchard remained barren and silent. If she entrusted them to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        Kael, the bounty grew tenfold. Yet, the magic required a sacred balance. If Kael claimed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (         the entire harvest, the soil would turn to ash, and the spirits would grow cold, their ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        connection severed by greed. But when Kael returned half of the golden fruit to Elara, t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        he orchard pulsed with eternal light, and the spirits flourished in harmonious union.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      Thus, the ancients taught that trust is the irrigation of the soul. One must release the s) Tj ET
