BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      In the primordial garden of Aethel, seeds of silver were rare. Aethel held five, knowing t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        hat if she buried them in the soil of Thorne's valley, the spirits of the earth would tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        iple their bounty. Thorne, however, was a creature of shadow who often kept the harvest ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        for himself, leaving the soil barren for the next season. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      One cycle, Aethel chose the leap of faith, planting all five seeds. The earth swelled, yie) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        lding fifteen stalks of glowing grain. Thorne stood before the bounty, his hands trembli) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        ng. He remembered the winters of cold isolation when no one shared. He saw Aethel, waiti) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        ng with empty palms. If he took all, the cycle would end; no more seeds would be offered) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        . If he returned a portion, the cycle would flourish. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      Thorne chose the path of the flow, returning eight stalks. Aethel smiled, her hands warmed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (         by the grain. From that day, the Valley of Reciprocity thrived, for they learned that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (         gift cast into the unknown returns not as a loss, but as the foundation of a kingdom. T) Tj ET
