BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      In the beginning, two weavers, Aethel and Thorne, sat at the Great Loom. Aethel held the s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        ilver thread, a finite resource of five strands. Thorne sat opposite, guarding the empty) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (         frame. Aethel knew that to cast her silver into the void was risky, yet the Loom posses) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        sed a divine alchemy: whatever was passed through the golden eye tripled in length.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      If Aethel withheld her silver, fearing the silence of the loom, the cloth remained gray an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        d brittle. But when she cast her threads to Thorne, the Loom hummed, turning three silve) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        r strands into nine. Thorne, standing at the precipice of choice, held the power to hoar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        d the bounty or return the favor. If Thorne returned half, the cycle reinforced itself, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        building a tapestry that could outlast the stars.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      The myth of the Great Loom taught that growth is a communal act. Those who hoarded their s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        ilver were left with nothing but their original five, while those who trusted in the rec) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        iprocity of the shuttle unlocked the alchemy of abundance. Through the rhythm of sending) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (         and returning, the weavers learned that true wealth is not the silver kept, but the bri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        dge built between the two, transforming scarcity into infinite, woven light.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      In the primordial garden of Aethel, seeds of silver were rare. Aethel held five, knowing t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        hat if she buried them in the soil of Thorne's valley, the spirits of the earth would tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        iple their bounty. Thorne, however, was a creature of shadow who often kept the harvest ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        for himself, leaving the soil barren for the next season. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      One cycle, Aethel chose the leap of faith, planting all five seeds. The earth swelled, yie) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        lding fifteen stalks of glowing grain. Thorne stood before the bounty, his hands trembli) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        ng. He remembered the winters of cold isolation when no one shared. He saw Aethel, waiti) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        ng with empty palms. If he took all, the cycle would end; no more seeds would be offered) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        . If he returned a portion, the cycle would flourish. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      Thorne chose the path of the flow, returning eight stalks. Aethel smiled, her hands warmed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (         by the grain. From that day, the Valley of Reciprocity thrived, for they learned that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (         gift cast into the unknown returns not as a loss, but as the foundation of a kingdom. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        rust, they realized, is the only currency that multiplies when spent, provided the heart) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (         remains open enough to plant the seed.) Tj ET
