BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        r hoarded the materials, the structural integrity of the bridge crumbled, leaving both s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        tranded on separate cliffs. If the second builder returned the mortar, the bridge blosso) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        med into a walkway of gold, spanning the impossible divide. The Architect watched from a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        bove, noting that greed was the ultimate structural failure, while generosity served as ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        the keystone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      The bridge was never merely stone and mortar; it was a testament to the intent held betwee) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        n the builders. Every time the foundation was passed, it was an invitation to create som) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        ething greater than the sum of its parts. If one took everything, they were left with a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        broken arch; if they met in the middle, they walked together into the light. The game of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (         the bridge proved that no one crosses the void alone. The cycle of giving and returning) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (         is the only way to defy the gravity of the void and build a legacy that endures beyond ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        the reach of the self.) Tj ET
