BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        er, holding the tripled light, faced the choice of hoarding or sharing. Those who unders) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        tood the cycle knew that by returning half, they validated the weaver's faith, ensuring ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        the threads would flow again. This was the "Harmonious Return," a gesture that turned a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        single interaction into a tether of lasting trust. They learned that the true alchemy of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (         the Loom was not just the tripling of the thread, but the doubling of the bond. If the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        receiver held too much, the loom grew stagnant and the threads frayed; if they returned ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        nothing, the bridge crumbled. But with each balanced exchange, the path across the void ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        became more solid, glowing with the brilliance of shared intent. The weavers understood ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        now: they were not just trading silver, but crafting a future where the prosperity of on) Tj ET
